# SHA256 digests for vendored Helm subchart tarballs.
#
# CI verifies each tarball in helm/rise/charts/ against this manifest after
# `helm dependency build` runs. Helm v4's Chart.lock only stores a single
# aggregate digest over the dependencies block (not per-tarball bytes), so a
# corrupted-but-correctly-named tarball would not be caught by `helm
# dependency build` alone. This file pins the exact bytes.
#
# Format: <sha256>  <filename>  (compatible with `shasum -a 256 -c`).
# Regenerate by running: cd helm/rise/charts && shasum -a 256 *.tgz > ../charts.sha256
# (then re-add the leading comment block).
54f8e723bc5b6f730d93489b9721abb1ce15c5d4d3ef80f1d11fe5983742fcf7  alloy-1.8.2.tgz
c8e5256c7a3dc32ef3aa994d8d5f41b010c2637c7a33f431d5c41d45dce31c29  loki-6.35.1.tgz
10497c22b8a35ca97ad87a06a3f7dd1b7045b7944c79e75a9c1b4427d05b842b  metacontroller-helm-4.17.2.tgz
